TI  - Inheritance of coat colour in the field spaniel dog
AU  - Robinson, R
T2  - GENETICS SELECTION EVOLUTION
AB  - The varieties of the field spaniel breed have the coat colours black, black and tan, liver, liver and tan; with or without roan colouration. Retrospective analysis of litter data reveals that the colours are produced by the agouti mutant alleles solid black (A(s)) and black and tan (a(t)), black pigmentation B, and liver brown b. Roan colouration is engendered by the gene combination s(p)s(p)TT. The breed is homozygous for long hair and the long coat enhances the effect of admixture of intermingled coloured and white hairs for the variety known as roan.
